.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt DERQ 1
.Os Darwin
.Sh NAME
.Nm derq
.Nd convert XML entitlements to V1 DER
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm query
.Fl f Cm xml
.Fl i Ar input
.Fl o Ar output
.Op Fl -raw
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The supported operation converts a single XML property list containing an
entitlements dictionary into its V1 DER representation.  No query statements
are supported; every argument after the options is rejected.
.Pp
Without
.Fl -raw
the output is the inner context-specific [16] dictionary.  With
.Fl -raw
the output is the complete V1 object: APPLICATION 16 containing INTEGER 1 and
that inner dictionary, matching the native macOS derq XML-input behavior.
.Pp
The input is read as an XML property list and must contain a dictionary at the
top level.  Malformed input is an error; it is never replaced with an empty
dictionary.  Unsupported subcommands and options are rejected; this tool does
not implement the Mach-O, csops, query-expression or DERQL interfaces of the
full Apple tool.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Cm xml
Select the input format.  Only
.Cm xml
is supported.
.It Fl i Ar input
Read from
.Ar input .
The value
.Dq -
means standard input.
.It Fl o Ar output
Write to
.Ar output .
The value
.Dq -
means standard output.
.It Fl -raw
Emit the outer V1 APPLICATION 16 object instead of only the inner [16]
dictionary.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
The input was converted and the complete output was written.
.It 1
The input could not be read or parsed, serialization failed, or the output
could not be completely written.
.It 65
The command line was invalid or requested an unsupported operation.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Convert the XML entitlements file and emit the inner dictionary:
.Dl % derq query -f xml -i application.xcent -o application.der
.Pp
Emit the complete V1 object to standard output:
.Dl % derq query -f xml -i application.xcent -o - --raw
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr codesign 1
